MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the example on the wiki, we use the factanal function from the stats package to run the EFA on the ldsc-derived S matrix. This doesn't use V, so there are no SEs. To get SEs I would recommend using the EFA solution to guide your specification of a CFA within Genomic SEM using usermodel, which uses V and outputs SEs. You can use SEs to get CIs the standard way.

